    {
      "record_id": "23202966",
      "title": "Binary consequences of relation-liveness automata lower bounds",
      "date": "2026-10-06",
      "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23202966",
      "url": "https://aleckriebel.com/research/binary-relation-liveness/",
      "description": "Explicit fixed-binary consequences of two attributed relation-liveness lower bounds, with exact compilers and full-word complement semantics.",
      "native_asset_order": [
        "README.md",
        "paper.pdf",
        "main.tex",
        "verification.zip"
      ],
      "whole_MAIN": {
        "bytes": 18217,
        "SHA256": "dea7de220d34fa434e6b71f8d7ebac969652f589c0037ed0a8ed9aa2c570bd8a"
      },
      "source_scholarly_metadata": {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "ScholarlyArticle",
        "headline": "Binary consequences of relation-liveness automata lower bounds",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Person",
          "name": "Alec Kriebel",
          "identifier": "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-9320-500X"
        },
        "datePublished": "2026-10-06",
        "identifier": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23202966",
        "url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23202966",
        "abstract": "We give explicit fixed-binary-alphabet consequences of OpenAI’s two relation-liveness lower bounds. Encoding each relation on h points by its h² adjacency bits gives a language recognized by a one-way nondeterministic automaton with Nₕ=(3h³−h)/2+2 states. Every equivalent two-way deterministic automaton, and every two-way nondeterministic automaton for its full binary complement, requires 2^{Ω(h)}=2^{Ω(Nₕ^(1/3))} states. We specify all transition rules, including an exact sh²-state pullback for an s-state binary target. The binary language rejects incomplete blocks; a fooling set proves that its one-way nondeterministic state complexity is Θ(h³). The exponential obstructions are inherited from the two upstream theorems; binary adjacency coding is established machinery.",
        "creativeWorkStatus": "Unrefereed preprint",
        "inLanguage": "en",
        "license": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
        "encoding": [
